{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991116-building-a-modern-standard-of-living-from-nothing","id":991116,"title":"Building a Modern Standard of Living from nothing.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T14:28:04-07:00","id":991116,"title":"Building a Modern Standard of Living from nothing.","content":"Suppose a mage was dropped into a vast empty space. The ground is paper white. So is the sky. The two seem to blend into one another in the distance. Perhaps it's a paradox realm, perhaps not. Who knows.<br /> <br /> What skills/spheres would they need to construct a modern standard of living?<br /> <br /> Presuming that....<br /> <br /> A.) This place has no node.<br /> B.) This place has no raw materials, the ground can be dug away, but it fades away into nothingness upon doing so.<br /> C.) This place has no strong Resonance of any kind.<br /> D.) This place experiences a night and day cycle much like any other.<br /> E.) The Mage has the minimum requisite tools to work their magic. Whatever those might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:06:52-07:00","id":991143,"title":"","content":"With Mind, Prime, and Matter you could just turn all thoughts into physical manifestations of reality.<br /> You could use Heart's Blood to get Quintessence out of your very own body, so as long as you don't mind waiting an hour or three between making things, you can in theory make everything you imagine real.<br /> <br /> Life would be useful for food, or at the very least to get around needing food.<br /> <br /> That's about it.<br /> Time could be useful if you're impatient and want your body to heal faster.<br /> Corr. is pretty much useless unless you start building so big that you need it to keep track of everything.<br /> Entropy doesn't have much function here,<br /> Forces would only really be necessary if you wanted to have electricity running, but nothing stops you from just creating a battery, wires, and devices with matter alone given enough time.<br /> Spirit would be outright pointless unless there were spirits in the area or the world was made of ephemera.<br /> If so, then all you need is Spirit to turn the world into whatever the heck you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:07:39-07:00","id":991214,"title":"","content":"Heart's Blood deals lethal damage, so you would need a day between points of Quintessence (unless they change healing rates dramatically in M20), and it cannot be accelerated by healing magic. We will assume that you have air, or else you will have a very, very short stay. <br /> <br /> The first problem is water. If you are physical, you need water, so you need Matter 2 and Prime 2, just to create the water that you need to survive (as well as a container to hold any water you create). The second problem is shelter, which can also be addressed with Matter 2 and Prime 2. The third problem is food, which requires Life 2 and Prime 2 to make edible materials. The fourth problem is sanitation, which can be addressed with Forces 2 and Prime 2 (or with Matter 2 and Prime 2 if you have Science or Survival). The fifth problem is warmth, which can be addressed with Forces 2 and Prime 2 (or Matter 2 and Prime 2 if you have Science or Survival). <br /> <br /> So, your character would need a minimum of Arete 2, Life 2, Matter 2, Prime 2, and Science 2 or Survival 2, all of which are doable for beginning characters. With careful planning, and enough time, you could create yourself a nice little garden in the middle of nowhere. You would not have any modern conveniences, and you would probably go mad from social isolation, but you would be able to survive until you died of old age, alone until the day you die. Strangely enough, it would be a fitting Paradox Realm for someone who had gained Paradox from immortality, so they would have sufficient magic to keep themselves alive, they would just never be able to leave the Paradox Realm until they permanently sacrificed their immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:09:16-07:00","id":991233,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> <br /> The problem with Prime 2 is you need your own source of Quintessence to do any of this stuff. Without using Heart's Blood, and without a node, you can't really do anything with Prime 2. Prime 5 would be required to call Quintessence out of the air.<br /> <br /> Fair point about Heart's Blood's Lethal Damage though. While yes you can't heal it with Life magic, you could conceivably increase recovery time by, instead of healing, accelerating your bodies natural healing factors via Time 3 Life 2. Increasing by a factor of 3, for example, would cut healing time down from a full day to about 8 hours.<br /> Also, Medicine knowledge can be used to speed up healing time quite considerably.<br /> If your Mage has Life 3 or Entropy 4, it's possibly they will not things like food or water to survive. All they have to do is magically sustain themselves with long term rituals.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone in this environment require a shelter? There is nothing but white all around them, nothing to shelter them from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:58:56-07:00","id":991294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991116-building-a-modern-standard-of-living-from-nothing?p=991233#post991233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a><br /> The problem with Prime 2 is you need your own source of Quintessence to do any of this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not require Quintessence to conjure items out of nothing with Prime 2 in M20. They do, however, fall under normal spell duration times by default, and permanency requires either a lot of successes, or Quintessence, depending on houserule. Per item.<br /> <br /> If the ST says 'Quintessence for permanency', then you need something like Heart's Blood, yes. But as Aya said, 1 point of lethal takes a DAY to heal. Not an hour <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Using time to speed that up would prrrrobably be paradox if done in a relevant manner, so you are exchanging one buildup for another. Although that one day healing time *might* be cut in half without it. Of course there is that little nagging voice in your head that also reminds you that you're speeding up your aging..<br /> <br /> <br /> ...last but not least <i>you need a paradigm</i> that supports creating all of that out of nothing, accelerating time or using Heart's Blood, and also supports creating all those items without in-depth knowledge of architecture, structural static, the materials and composition, how to make a battery etc., *and* also says that it's okay to just do all that because the Mage is too lazy to put mundane work into it.<br /> Heh. That paradigm issue might be the hardest part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-22-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T01:42:12-07:00","id":991309,"title":"","content":"According to assumption E.) it is beneficial if the mage in question is a technomancer with high minimum requirements in instruments (tuned car, computer, generator etc.)<br /> <br /> A Dreamspeaker with Spirit 3 and Mind 3, Arete 3 and a Demesne and/or Lucid Dreaming would manage quite well I guess.<br /> The ability to walk in (ephemeral) flesh into one's own Dreamrealm and find sustenance there is perfect for this scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T05:01:34-07:00","id":991343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991116-building-a-modern-standard-of-living-from-nothing?p=991294#post991294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do not require Quintessence to conjure items out of nothing with Prime 2 in M20. They do, however, fall under normal spell duration times by default, and permanency requires either a lot of successes, or Quintessence, depending on houserule. Per item.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, M20 really changed up the Prime sphere a lot...<br /> It's almost unrecognisable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:25:48-07:00","id":991366,"title":"","content":"In the described scenario it could be that a simple Prime 2 channeling is not sufficient. Simply because there is not enough ambient quint available (no node, no resonance, etc. just air, plain ground and you).<br /> <br /> In my games you can substitute the Prime 2 requirement in an effect with 1 point of quint.<br /> Quintessence is more rare and vastly more powerful at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:21:43-07:00","id":991502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991116-building-a-modern-standard-of-living-from-nothing?p=991343#post991343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, M20 really changed up the Prime sphere a lot...<br /> It's almost unrecognisable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised was, AFAIK, the only edition that enforced spending Quintessence to conjure things.<br /> The rest of Prime is..pretty much the same, unless I'm not remembering something.<br /> <br /> What you *do* require Quintessence for, is to create something like fire, and then have it fuel itself for longer than a turn. if you don't have something combustable you toss it at, you need to keep it going with Quint. Same goes for any other longer-lasting generation of energy, like electricity out of nothing, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:56:29-07:00","id":991568,"title":"","content":"That is one of the reasons to have Matter. It is easier to create coal and burn it than to create an orb of fire that exists without fuel for a prolonged period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:19:53-07:00","id":991581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991116-building-a-modern-standard-of-living-from-nothing?p=991502#post991502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised was, AFAIK, the only edition that enforced spending Quintessence to conjure things.<br /> The rest of Prime is..pretty much the same, unless I'm not remembering something.<br /> <br /> What you *do* require Quintessence for, is to create something like fire, and then have it fuel itself for longer than a turn. if you don't have something combustable you toss it at, you need to keep it going with Quint. Same goes for any other longer-lasting generation of energy, like electricity out of nothing, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though M20 also did away with Tass for Wonder crafting.<br /> <br /> Shame, I like Quintessence being a necessity for creating stuff out of nothing via Prim 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}